As discussed, the total development cost for the complete Diabetes Care App will be ₹4 lakh.

To make the development process smooth and practical, we can divide the project into two phases.

Before starting the development, we will sign a formal agreement/contract that clearly defines the scope of work, deliverables, timelines, ownership, and payment structure so that everything remains transparent and well-documented for both sides.

Phase 1 – MVP Development:
In the first phase, we will develop and launch the MVP (Minimum Viable Product) with all the core and essential features required for the app to function properly. This will allow you to start testing the platform with real users and present the product to potential investors.
The cost for this phase will be ₹1.2 lakh.

Phase 2 – Full App Development:
In the second phase, we will continue the development and add all the remaining advanced features, enhancements, and integrations, leading to the complete version of the application. The remaining amount from the ₹4 lakh budget can be paid during this phase when we proceed with the full release.

Since user health data is extremely crucial, the application will be developed with secure data handling practices and a scalable architecture, ensuring that the platform can grow smoothly as the number of users increases.

We will also provide full source code ownership to you, and the system will be designed to ensure that your application data remains secure and fully under your control.

This phased approach allows you to launch faster with a working product, validate the idea in the market, and then scale the application with additional features in the next version.', 'Completed', NULL, '2026-03-10 10:19:33.399+00', '2026-03-10 10:19:35.261125+00', '2026-03-10 10:19:35.261125+00');
